      <Desc>WE PARTNERED WITH THE SURFRIDER FOUNDATION TO ADVANCE THE "LIGHTER THAN AIR" MYLAR AND LATEX BALLOON BAN IN SAN DIEGO COUNTY AND LAUNCHED A DATA COLLECTION INITIATIVE ON OUR WEBSITE TO TRACK MYLAR AND LATEX BALLOON WASTE. WE HAVE ALSO ACTIVELY BEEN EDUCATING THE COMMUNITY ABOUT THIS ONGOING ISSUE VIA SOCIAL MEDIA WITH MUCH SUPPORT. WE PROMOTED SUSTAINABLE FISHING BY SUPPORTING CCA'S WHITE SEABASS TOURNAMENT, CONTRIBUTING TO HUBBS-SEAWORLD'S RESEARCH EFFORTS AND EDUCATING THE PUBLIC ABOUT WHAT IS POSSIBLE WITH PROPER FISHERIES MANAGEMENT. WE ALSO TAGGED AND RELEASED OVER 30 STRIPED MARLIN FOR NOAA AND THE BILLFISH FOUNDATION TO SUPPORT STUDIES ON MIGRATION AND SPAWNING PATTERNS. THE R/V PILAR TEAM PLACED 3RD IN THE PRESTIGIOUS BISBEE'S BLACK &amp; BLUE MARLIN TOURNAMENT, LANDING A 493-POUND BLUE MARLIN. THIS ACCOMPLISHMENT GAINED US MUCH RESPECT AMONG OUR PEERS IN THE SPORTFISHING COMMUNITY, BRINGING GREATER AWARENESS TO OUR MISSION OF MARINE CONSERVATION AND RESPONSIBLE FISHING. TO LEAD BY EXAMPLE, WE DONATED OUR CATCH TO A LOCAL FAMILY, ENSURING NO FISH WENT TO WASTE."</Desc>
